-- Selective per-player looting for collect-X quest drops (R18 / P7.21).
--
-- Blizzard progressively made collect-X quest items lootable by every eligible party member rather
-- than once per corpse, and backported that convention to WotLK Classic. This reproduces it for the
-- category Blizzard actually revised, rather than flagging every quest item the way a blanket
-- approach would.
--
-- ITEM_FLAG_MULTI_DROP (0x800) is already honoured by the core: LootMgr.cpp maps it to `freeforall`,
-- which fills a per-player loot list. This is therefore a data change only.
--
-- Scope, measured against this world database:
--   * 1907 quest-required items drop from creatures
--   *  818 already carry the flag -- overwhelmingly SINGLE-drop quest items, not collect-X
--   *  776 collect-X items (RequiredItemCount > 1) drop from creatures and are NOT flagged
--   *   35 collect-X items are already flagged
-- So this category is essentially untouched and does not overlap the existing flags.
--
-- Every row below is quest-required with a count above one, drops from a named creature, and is not
-- already flagged. One row per item with the quest and creature that justify it, so the change can
-- be reviewed item by item rather than taken on trust.
--
-- Reversal: UPDATE item_template SET Flags = Flags & ~0x800 WHERE entry IN (...the same ids...);
--
-- Not included: items whose only sources are instanced, and single-drop quest items. Confirming
-- these against WotLK Classic's own flags is still worth doing when that data is available -- see
-- PLAN P7.21 -- but the local filter stands on its own.

UPDATE `item_template` SET `Flags` = `Flags` | 0x800 WHERE `entry` = 723; -- Goretusk Liver (quest 22, from Bellygrub)
